1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,178
See an outfit you love?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,072
Just snap it.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,663
Meta AI takes it from there.

4
00:00:08,683 --> 00:00:12,576
SAM finds every garment, and Muse Spark reads the details.

5
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:15,164
A polka-dot maxi dress, found.

6
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,476
And one tap to shop similar styles.

7
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:21,795
But most of the looks you love aren't on the street.

8
00:00:21,815 --> 00:00:22,996
They're in your feed.

9
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:25,344
So we built Rewear for Chrome.

10
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:28,620
Hover over any photo, and click “Shop this look”.

11
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:33,582
Rewear opens by itself, and Meta AI gets to work.

12
00:00:37,967 --> 00:00:40,313
Eight pieces, across all three outfits.

13
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:46,570
Muse Image then previews every piece, clearly labeled as AI.

14
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:51,739
Tap any piece to shop similar styles on Google, Bing or the web.

15
00:00:54,383 --> 00:00:57,099
Under the hood, three Meta models work together.

16
00:00:57,133 --> 00:01:00,994
SAM 3.1 segments every garment, pixel by pixel.

17
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,753
Muse Spark 1.3 reads each piece:

18
00:01:03,773 --> 00:01:06,412
its type, cut, color and fabric.

19
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:13,092
And Muse Image 1.0 previews the complete garment, always labeled as AI.

20
00:01:13,983 --> 00:01:16,504
Every photo in a feed is shopping intent:

21
00:01:16,524 --> 00:01:20,221
one click for shoppers, new revenue for creators and brands,

22
00:01:20,241 --> 00:01:23,663
and native outfit search for Facebook and Instagram.

23
00:01:24,483 --> 00:01:27,325
It’s honest by design, and it’s tested:

24
00:01:27,345 --> 00:01:33,636
90 of 100 garments identified on a fixed benchmark, and over 1,500 automated tests.

25
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:37,523
Rewear Studio. See it. Find it. Buy it.
